  "key_observations_html": "<aside class=\"crypto-story-callout\" aria-labelledby=\"key-obs-callout-title\"><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__title\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" id=\"key-obs-callout-title\">Key observations</p><ul class=\"crypto-story-callout__list\"><li><strong>TMMF printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed value near $13.13B (+1.9% 30D) leaves tokenized-cash balances largely range-bound\u2014the market story this week is more about issuer and distribution news than a shift in AUM. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/tradfi-and-fintech/tempo-earn-embedded-stablecoin-yield-deel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tempo Launches Embedded Yield Product for Platforms, Starting With Deel</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>A global regulatory arbitrage map is emerging:</strong> distributed value clusters into distinct compliance regimes\u2014<strong>U.S. Reg D</strong> ~41% of population AUM (e.g. BUIDL, iBENJI); <strong>U.S. Reg S</strong> ~39% of population AUM (e.g. USYC, USDY); <strong>U.S. mutual fund (N-1A)</strong> ~6% of population AUM (e.g. WTGXX). Issuers appear to anchor products in familiar safe harbors rather than one global standard. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/08/16/the-sec-meeting-that-wasn-t-state-of-crypto\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The SEC meeting that wasn&#x27;t: State of Crypto</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Multi-chain footprints are a distribution signal:</strong> Funds listing many networks with thin holder counts usually signal jurisdictional or distribution reach, not deep secondary liquidity on every chain. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/dartmouth-endowment-crypto-investments-btc-eth-sol-dropped?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Dartmouth endowment\u2019s crypto exposure drops by $2M amid falling prices</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Rates still matter as much as product and chain choice:</strong> Rate and money-market moves can reshape fund-level inflows as quickly as any chain or product launch story. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/cftc-ai-compute-futures-cme-october-launch?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CFTC seeks public input on AI compute futures contracts as CME eyes October launch</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Issuer strategies are splitting into two models:</strong> <em>Institutional cash rail</em> programs (low holder counts, large AUM per holder\u2014e.g. USYC, BUIDL, iBENJI, USTB) vs <em>global yield / distribution</em> products (broader holder bases, retail- or UCITS-friendly framing\u2014e.g. USDY, WTGXX, BENJI, USTBL). These behave like different businesses under the same \"tokenized MMF\" label. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/08/17/saylor-says-share-buyback-isn-t-a-priority-as-it-builds-its-usd4-8-billion-cash-reserve-though-a-possibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Saylor says share buyback isn\u2019t priority as Strategy builds $4.8 billion cash reserve</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Observations rank fund-level and network aggregates on this page against recent tokenization and money-market headlines. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></aside><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
